i'm in grund hayden near berlin where  elon musk is gearing up to beat the  german automakers at what they're best  at  perfect in car manufacturing  tesla already leads on batteries and  softwares but when it comes to actually  making the car the common belief was  that the german automakers vw and bmw  would quickly beat the new upstart  because of their superior manufacturing  chops  elon musk believes he can prove them  wrong and he'll do it right here in  their backyard  the plant which musk hopes will start  producing model wise before the end of  the year is supposed to revolutionize  car production by churning out an ev  three times faster than his german  rivals can if musk can deliver he'll  take giant strides toward more  affordable evs further threatening the  mass market manufacturers  key to his plan is the gigapress several  vast die casting machines each weighing  about three times as much as the statue  of liberty these machines take molten  aluminum to spit out much of the chassis  in a single piece thus removing the need  for 200 industrial robots and a 60 part  assembly  tesla also designed a new battery pack  linking the cars front and rear on the  bodies so instead of a pack that's  bolted to the chassis with lots of metal  parts it instead functions as a key  structural element of the vehicle that  makes production faster and the car  lighter resulting in a bigger range and  finally tesla says its paint job is  unique because it can apply 13 layers of  varnish thinner than a human hair there  are risks to mast efficiency push  he has said that tesla will be trying  lots of new tech at queen hider and he  has warned of significant production  risks because of it  also tesla is still waiting for final  approval from local authorities for the  site  german car makers are nevertheless  watching very closely what happens here  in greenheider and some are already  preparing to strike back volkswagen has  said it wants to build a new eevee  factory in wolfsburg at its headquarters  to make 250 000 cars a year and it wants  to catch up with tesla on production  time  still if musk succeeds here at  clenheider this factory could be the  benchmark for ev production for some  time this is how we move i'm stefan  nicola for more contact like this follow  us on your favorite platforms
 

